    \u0E09\u0E1A\u0E31\u0E1A\u0E41\u0E23\u0E01"
  mailShopLevel: 1
  mailReputation: 380
  chef: {fileID: 11400000, guid: cd96477d5695e8349a71dcd12e8bd8d2, type: 2}
  letterBody: 'Hola, amigo,


    My grandson reads restaurant reviews from all over
    the world, and yours made him laugh: "Tacos in the countryside, made by someone
    who isn''t even Mexican." Then he said they were good. So now I must help you
    make them better.


    I am Rosa Delgado, a cocinera from Oaxaca. Tacos were
    the first thing I ever sold, from a basket on my head, when I was twelve.


    Warm
    the tortillas until they puff. Seasoned beef, fresh tomato, crisp lettuce, a
    squeeze of lime. Two tortillas if the filling is generous.


    Food is for
    sharing. Never forget it.'
